course: dictionary
lesson: 12641
title: A dispenser gives out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dispenser is a machine or container that gives out a fixed amount of something when you press, pull or push it. The word comes from «dispense», which means to give out. So a dispenser is something that gives things out.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Sam pressed the soap dispenser, and one squirt of soap came out.» Pressed and came out tell you the dispenser gives out soap. Always ask: what does it give out, and how does it do it?
explain: You can meet dispensers in many places. «Mia pulled the tape dispenser and tore off a strip.» «The cash dispenser at the bank gave out money.» Each one gives out a set amount each time you use it, so it is a dispenser.
fact: Dispenser is a noun. One is a dispenser, and more than one is dispensers.
fact: A dispenser is a machine or container that gives out a fixed amount of something when you press, pull or push it.
fact: Soap dispensers, water dispensers, tape dispensers and cash dispensers are all examples.
fact: A cash dispenser is another name for a cash machine at a bank.
fact: In hygiene lessons, use the soap dispenser and wash your hands well.
exercise: «Each time Sam pressed the soap dispenser, one squirt of soap came out.» What is a dispenser? | *A machine that gives out a fixed amount | A bag for carrying books | A loud bell that rings at break
exercise: Which of these is a dispenser you might find in a school toilet? | *A soap dispenser | A cookery book | A bus timetable | A garden hose
exercise: «Lily pulled a strip of tape from the tape dispenser.» What does the tape dispenser give out? | Soap | *Tape | Water | Cash
test: «The water dispenser in the corridor gave Ravi a small cup of water.» What does a dispenser give out? | Soap | Tape | Cups | *Water
test: Which phrase means a cash machine at a bank? | tape dispenser | water dispenser | soap dispenser | *cash dispenser
exam: Which of these describes a dispenser best? | A school bell | *A machine or container that gives out a fixed amount when you press, pull or push it | A kind of weather | A bag that holds your lunch
